#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `reading F4.1 C` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 15)

#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `reading F4.1 B` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `reading F4.1 C` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 16)

-- The same difference through the duty to disclose. A payment on 14 March 2025 is outside A and B and inside C; one on 15 March 2026 is inside B only.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.1 B` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.1 C` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2026 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.1 B` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2026 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.1 C` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2026 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `reading F4.1 C` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`) FALSE

§§ `F4.2 -- which day is the date of the application`

#ASSERT `Art 11 the date of the application` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 11 the date of the application` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 20
-- The windows follow: A runs 1 March 2025 to 28 February 2026, B runs 20 March 2025 to 19 March 2026; so the payment of 10 March 2026 is outside the first and inside the second.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2025 3 1), (YMD 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2025 3 20), (YMD 2026 3 19))
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026`
-- The same anchor starts the period an Order may set for the decision (P7): 30 days from 1 March 2026 end on 31 March; from 20 March they end on 19 April.
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 19
-- An application that is not yet complete has no date under reading B: the model refuses by name; under reading A it has its lodging date.
#ASSERT `Art 11 the date of the application` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11 the date of the application` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` BECAUSE "no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `reading F4.2 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` BECAUSE "no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete"
#ASSERT `F4.2 reading A: the date of the application is the day it is lodged` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `F4.2 reading B: the date of the application is the day it becomes complete` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 20
#ASSERT REFUSED `F4.2 reading B: the date of the application is the day it becomes complete` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` BECAUSE "no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete"

-- The tension between F4.2 reading A and F4.3 reading A (FRAGMENT-G4.md, F4.2): while an application does not comply, no duty to decide arises, yet an Order's period would already be running from the day it was lodged.
-- Both facts are asserted: the last day is computed, and the Commissioner has no duty on the application.
`the application lodged on 1 March 2026 without a copy of the constitution` MEANS `Application for registration` WITH
    dates IS `dates: lodged on 1 March 2026, not yet complete`
    `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `particulars: everything provided, paragraph (iii) does not apply`
    `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `documents: no copy of the constitution`
    `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `financial details: nothing further required`
    `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `other requirements: none arise`
    `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 without a copy of the constitution` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the base case` `but with the application as` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 without a copy of the constitution`) EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`

§§ `F4.3 -- an application that does not comply`

-- The case of trap T10 (B): the six matters are found, but the copy of the constitution (Article 11(2)(b)) is missing.
-- A (taken): neither duty arises. B: the Commissioner must refuse. C (Article 11(5) read on its own words): the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone, which are found, so no duty arises.
`the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` MEANS `the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)
`the case where a matter is not found and the copy of the constitution is missing` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)) `but with the name as` TRUE
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 C`) EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
-- Where a matter is not found as well, the readings A and C part: C refuses, because Article 11(5) says "If not so satisfied" and does not repeat the condition of compliance.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a matter is not found and the copy of the constitution is missing` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a matter is not found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a matter is not found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 C`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- The readings alone, over the four combinations of compliance and the six matters (complies, found).
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading A: a non-complying application leaves the Commissioner with no duty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading B: a non-complying application must be refused` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `F4.3 reading C: the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- The decision of Article 11 the other groups read: on reading B the missing copy is a refusal.
#ASSERT `the decision in` (`the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 B`) EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` (`the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.3 B`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` `the case where the six matters are found and the copy of the constitution is missing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)


§§ `F4.4 -- the duty to register against the bars on granting (trap T10)`

-- A reported fitness issue is undetermined (Article 19(9)(c)), or the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered (Article 20(1)(c)); the six matters are found and the applicant complies.
-- A (taken): the bars displace the duty to register. B: Article 11(4) prevails. C: the model refuses to choose.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` EQUALS `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the duty in` (`the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 C`) BECAUSE "Articles 11(4), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) conflict and this encoding does not choose between them"
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the duty in` (`the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 C`) BECAUSE "Articles 11(4), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) conflict and this encoding does not choose between them"
-- On B the decision of Article 11 is to register in both cases; on A there is no decision under Article 11(4) or (5); on C the model refuses.
#ASSERT `the decision in` (`the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 B`) EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the decision in` (`the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 C`)
-- A bar does not matter where the duty before it is not to register: a refusal or no duty is the same on every reading.
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the name is undesirable` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the name is undesirable` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 C`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the copy of the constitution is missing` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.4 C`) EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
-- The readings alone: (before, the 19(9)(c) bar, the court order).
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading A: a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register` `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading B: the duty to register prevails once its six matters hold` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT REFUSED `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` `the Commissioner must register the applicant` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `F4.4 reading C: the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`


§§ `F4.5 -- is a formerly registered charity another registered charity`

-- A proposed name identical to the registered name of a charity that has since been deregistered (its entry is in the historic section).
-- A (taken): Article 1 defines a registered charity as one entered in the general or the restricted section, so the entry is not another registered charity's name. B: it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of a charity that has been deregistered`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.5 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of a charity that has been deregistered`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.5 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the restricted section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.5 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the restricted section`))
#ASSERT `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` `entered in the general section`
#ASSERT `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` `entered in the restricted section`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` `an applicant for registration`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.5 reading A: only an entity entered in the general or the restricted section is a registered charity` `not on the register`
#ASSERT `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
#ASSERT `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` `entered in the general section`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` `an applicant for registration`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.5 reading B: a formerly registered entity in the historic section counts as well` `not on the register`

§§ `F4.6 -- a year before 29 February`

-- Lodged and complete on 29 February 2028 (a leap day). The same day one year earlier does not exist.
-- A (taken): `add years` gives 28 February 2027. B: the lenient Date gives 1 March 2027.
`the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` MEANS `the base application with dates` `dates: lodged and complete on 29 February 2028`
#ASSERT `F4.6 reading A: a year before` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `F4.6 reading B: a year before` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `the default reading` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `reading F4.6 B` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
-- The two readings agree on every day that exists a year earlier.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `the default reading` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `reading F4.6 B` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `the default reading` (YMD 2028 3 1) EQUALS `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` `reading F4.6 B` (YMD 2028 3 1)
-- The windows ending on 28 February 2028 (reading F4.1 A): from 28 February 2027 under A, from 1 March 2027 under B.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `the default reading` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 2 28), (YMD 2028 2 28))
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `reading F4.6 B` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 3 1), (YMD 2028 2 28))
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` (YMD 2027 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `reading F4.6 B` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` (YMD 2027 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` (YMD 2027 2 27)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `reading F4.6 B` `the application lodged and complete on 29 February 2028` (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- Reading B of F4.1 (the twelve months ending on the day of the application) starts the day after the anniversary: 1 March 2027 with the clamp, 2 March 2027 with the roll.
#ASSERT `F4.1 reading B: the twelve months ending on the day of the application` `the default reading` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 3 1), (YMD 2028 2 29))
#ASSERT `F4.1 reading B: the twelve months ending on the day of the application` `reading F4.6 B` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 3 2), (YMD 2028 2 29))
-- Reading C does not take a year back from a day, so it does not depend on F4.6.
#ASSERT `F4.1 reading C: the twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2027 2 1), (YMD 2028 1 31))

§§ `F4.7 -- which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares`

-- The proposed name is, in the Commissioner's opinion, the same as a name that another charity in the general section has as its alternative registered name, or has given up (a previous registered name).
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 C` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `an alternative registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `an alternative registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 C` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `an alternative registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `a previous registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 B` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `a previous registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `reading F4.7 C` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `a previous registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading A: the registered name and the alternative registered names` `the registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading A: the registered name and the alternative registered names` `an alternative registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.7 reading A: the registered name and the alternative registered names` `a previous registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading B: the registered name only` `the registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.7 reading B: the registered name only` `an alternative registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.7 reading B: the registered name only` `a previous registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading C: every name entered, previous names included` `the registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading C: every name entered, previous names included` `an alternative registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.7 reading C: every name entered, previous names included` `a previous registered name`

§§ `F4.8 -- a previous registered name of the charity itself`

-- Hope Foundation Limited has changed its registered name from Hope Foundation; the register keeps Hope Foundation as a previous registered name (Article 8(3)(l)). The charity uses it.
-- A (taken): the previous name is not one of its registered names, so it must pass sub-paragraph (b); unrelated, it is not permitted. B: it is still a registered name.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `reading F4.8 B` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name`
-- Related and acceptable in its context, the previous name passes sub-paragraph (b) on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is related and not undesirable in its context`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `reading F4.8 B` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is related and not undesirable in its context`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.8 reading A: only the names registered now` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name`
#ASSERT `F4.8 reading B: the previous registered names as well` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name`
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation")) AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `reading F4.8 B` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` `the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation")) AT 5

§§ `F4.9 -- counting the period for the Commissioner's decision`

-- An Order allows 30 days from the date of the application, 1 March 2026 (the application is lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete; the reading of F4.2 is the lodging date).
-- A (taken): the period starts the day after, so the last day is 31 March. B: 1 March is the first day, so the last day is 30 March.
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `reading F4.9 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 30
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `reading F4.9 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `reading F4.9 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `reading F4.9 B` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading A: the last day of the period` (YMD 2026 3 1) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading B: the last day of the period` (YMD 2026 3 1) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 30
-- A period of one day: A ends on the day after the anchor, B on the anchor itself.
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading A: the last day of the period` (YMD 2026 3 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading B: the last day of the period` (YMD 2026 3 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- Across the end of a month and of a leap February: 30 days from 15 February 2028 end on 16 March 2028 (A) or 15 March 2028 (B).
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading A: the last day of the period` (YMD 2028 2 15) 30 EQUALS YMD 2028 3 16
#ASSERT `F4.9 reading B: the last day of the period` (YMD 2028 2 15) 30 EQUALS YMD 2028 3 15

§§ `F4.10 -- reasonable time and as soon as practicable, for the guidance (set together with F2.4 of group G2)`

-- Article 5(7) as applied: the guidance was issued on 1 January 2026 and the copy provided to the Minister on 1 March 2026, 59 days later (January has 31 days and February 28).
-- A (taken): whatever the caller determines, the dates ignored. B: the days between the two dates against the number the caller supplies.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `the default reading` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `the default reading` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 90)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `reading F4.10 B` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 30)
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 90)
-- The boundary: 59 days is within 59 and not within 58.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 59)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (JUST 58)
-- The Law gives no number: reading B without one refuses, by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) NOTHING BECAUSE "no number of days for a reasonable time after issuing or amending the guidance is in the Law"
#ASSERT `F4.10 reading A: the copy was provided within a reasonable time` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F4.10 reading A: the copy was provided within a reasonable time` FALSE
-- Article 5(8) as applied: the Minister received the guidance and the report on 1 June 2026 and laid the copy on 15 June 2026, 14 days later.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `the default reading` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (JUST 7)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `reading F4.10 B` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (JUST 7)
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (JUST 14)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (JUST 13)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `reading F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) NOTHING BECAUSE "no number of days for as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the guidance is in the Law"

§§ `F4.11 -- the payee who is a governor`

-- Carl was a governor when paid on 1 December 2025 and has since ceased to be one; Dina was not a governor when paid on 1 December 2025 and has since become one. The application is lodged on 15 March 2026.
-- A (taken): a governor when paid. B: a governor on the date of the application.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `the default reading` `the base application` `payment of 600 to Carl on 1 December 2025, who has since ceased to be a governor`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `reading F4.11 B` `the base application` `payment of 600 to Carl on 1 December 2025, who has since ceased to be a governor`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `the default reading` `the base application` `payment of 700 to Dina on 1 December 2025, who became a governor later`
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `reading F4.11 B` `the base application` `payment of 700 to Dina on 1 December 2025, who became a governor later`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment to a former governor made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.11 B` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment to a former governor made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment to a later governor made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `reading F4.11 B` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment to a later governor made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `F4.11 reading A: the payee was a governor when the payment was made` `payment of 600 to Carl on 1 December 2025, who has since ceased to be a governor`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.11 reading B: the payee is a governor on the date of the application` `payment of 600 to Carl on 1 December 2025, who has since ceased to be a governor`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.11 reading A: the payee was a governor when the payment was made` `payment of 700 to Dina on 1 December 2025, who became a governor later`
#ASSERT `F4.11 reading B: the payee is a governor on the date of the application` `payment of 700 to Dina on 1 December 2025, who became a governor later`

§§ `F4.12 -- "applies or should be applied" in Article 11(4)(f)`

-- The Regulations prescribe a ground on which an application MAY be refused. Its circumstances are present, but the Commissioner does not consider that it should be applied.
-- A (taken): "should be applied" governs a ground of discretionary refusal, so the matter (f) holds and the Commissioner must register. B: "applies" is not qualified, so a ground whose circumstances are present defeats the matter and the Commissioner must refuse.
`the case where the circumstances of a ground of discretionary refusal are present but the ground should not be applied` MEANS `the base case` `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `the default reading` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `reading F4.12 B` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the circumstances of a ground of discretionary refusal are present but the ground should not be applied` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` (`the case where the circumstances of a ground of discretionary refusal are present but the ground should not be applied` `but with the reading as` `reading F4.12 B`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- A ground of mandatory refusal that applies, or a ground of discretionary refusal that should be applied, defeats the matter on both readings; with no ground the matter holds on both.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `reading F4.12 B` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a mandatory prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `reading F4.12 B` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `reading F4.12 B` `the base findings`
#ASSERT `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` `the base findings`
#ASSERT `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a mandatory prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `F4.12 reading A: no ground of mandatory refusal applies and no ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` `the base findings`
#ASSERT NOT `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground whose circumstances are present as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a mandatory prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `F4.12 reading B: no prescribed ground has its circumstances present` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground as` TRUE)

